# Every Python test module in scripts/avatar/, 2026-09-11, one process each,
# all on the tree this commit leaves behind. module, tests, wall clock, exit
# code, unittest summary.
#
# retarget_test.py is a gate script rather than a unittest module: it prints its
# own PASS across 10 clips and exits 0, so it reports no test count.
#
# dressup_test.py reports 11 here and reported 8 in the run this replaces. Its
# `unittest.main()` guard sat above the last two classes in the file, so those
# 3 tests had never run, and 8 of 8 passing prints exactly like a full run. The
# guard now sits at the end; all 11 pass. Every module in this directory was
# checked for the same defect by comparing what running the file reports against
# what unittest.TestLoader collects from it, and this was the only one that
# disagreed. That is why the total is 443 and not 440.
#
# The timings are lower than the earlier run's throughout (cover_test 927s to
# 449s, pierce_test 261s to 59s) because that one was taken with the disk at
# 100%; see verify-vrm1-0910.md section 7.
